; The glides at a segment's ends. Eight cards a frame in: a, b, uu and g from the chooser, wl and wr from the
; framer, and its segment's pte and nts (from spread); per frame six out (a, b, uu, gn, go, w) for the filter
; machines. A frame with glides (g) at the segment's start (wl, and a sound before: pte) glides from halfway between
; pte and a: gn pte, go a, weight wl; at its end (wr, and a sound after: nts) from halfway between b and nts.
; Otherwise gn = go = a and the weight is 10, all the frame's own.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frm     INP   a        03-29: a frame, and its segment's pte and nts
  04                    INP   b
  05                    INP   uu
  06                    INP   g
  07                    INP   wl
  08                    INP   wr
  09                    INP   pte
  10                    INP   nts
  11                    CLA   a
  12                    STO   gn
  13                    STO   go
  14                    CLA   c10
  15                    STO   w
  16                    CLA   g
  17                    SUB   00
  18                    TAC   out
  19                    CLA   wl
  20                    SUB   00
  21                    TAC   rt
  22                    CLA   pte
  23                    SUB   00
  24                    TAC   rt
  25                    CLA   pte
  26                    STO   gn
  27                    CLA   wl
  28                    STO   w
  29                    JMP   out
  30            rt      CLA   wr       30-41: a glide at the end
  31                    SUB   00
  32                    TAC   out
  33                    CLA   nts
  34                    SUB   00
  35                    TAC   out
  36                    CLA   nts
  37                    STO   gn
  38                    CLA   b
  39                    STO   go
  40                    CLA   wr
  41                    STO   w
  42            out     OUT   a        42-60: the cards
  43                    OUT   b
  44                    OUT   uu
  45                    OUT   gn
  46                    OUT   go
  47                    OUT   w
  48                    JMP   frm
  49            pte     DATA  0
  50            nts     DATA  0
  51            a       DATA  0
  52            b       DATA  0
  53            uu      DATA  0
  54            g       DATA  0
  55            wl      DATA  0
  56            wr      DATA  0
  57            gn      DATA  0
  58            go      DATA  0
  59            w       DATA  0
  60            c10     DATA  10
